      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T22:35:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is mainly because at least for the Android phone, the privacy mode is by default enabled. As a result, the host address is always resolvable random. I don\u0027t see a use case when the android needs to run with a public address + privacy mode, or non-privacy mode + a random address. But for Chrome OS, we currently have non-privacy mode + public address, so we need a transition state to fully migrate to the same as android.",
      "parentUuid": "95a82394_befe18da",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
